      "sequence_position": 2,
      "problem": "Solve $f(t)=0$ where $f(t)=\\frac{t-3}{{t}^{2}+6t+5}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we factor $f(t),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =\\frac{t-3}{{t}^{2}+6t+5} \\\\  & =\\frac{t-3}{(t+5)(t+1)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThere are no common factors in the numerator and denominator, so we set the numerator equal to zero and solve for $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t-3 & =0 \\\\ t & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to $f(t)=0$ is $t=3.$",
